Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.98,0:00:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">The fastest courtship upon record occurred{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.24,0:00:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}during the markedly wet season of 1804,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.66,0:00:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when Miss Mary Leopold secured a betrothal{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.24,0:00:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}over a plate{\i0}\N{\i1}of sugared almonds and licorice{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.54,0:00:36.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in just four and a half minutes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.17,0:00:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, Miss Leopold{\i0}\N{\i1}and her new husband would leave London{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.55,0:00:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}mere hours after their wedding.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.01,0:00:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Reason unknown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.43,0:00:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of all{\i0}\N{\i1}that I have imparted to you, dear reader,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.43,0:00:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}there is but one bit of wisdom{\i0}\N{\i1}you must heed most.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.02,0:00:59.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One can never know the truth{\i0}\N{\i1}of a marriage hiding behind closed doors.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.98,0:01:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Beware indeed, blushing newlyweds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.36,0:01:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know not the future that awaits.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.16,0:01:09.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will there be hardship{\i0}<span style="style1">…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.45,0:01:12.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't you touch me. Stay away!{\i0}\N{\i1}Just leave me alone!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.45,0:01:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…or indignity?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.62,0:01:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[King George] Go away! Leave me alone!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.22,0:01:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or will one's future see{\i0}\N{\i1}the rarest accomplishment of all,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.01,0:01:34.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a true love match?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.31,0:01:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As for which of these fates await{\i0}\N{\i1}the eager matches of the season of 1813,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.15,0:01:45.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}only two things will tell…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.74,0:01:46.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Time,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.78,0:01:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and, as always,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.70,0:01:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}this author.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.20,0:01:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are permitted to smile, Your Graces.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.54,0:01:55.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.91,0:02:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Might you both move a bit closer as well?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.29,0:02:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.34,0:02:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Better.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.59,0:02:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once this portrait business is settled,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall quit London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.93,0:02:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tonight, perhaps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.89,0:02:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And draw new whispers{\i0}\N{\i1}about the state of our marriage?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.43,0:02:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would prefer otherwise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.27,0:02:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now that we know I am not with child,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.48,0:02:23.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you should depart London{\i0}\N{\i1}at the end of the season,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.82,0:02:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with the rest of the ton, as planned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.15,0:02:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-It is but a few more days.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon] Very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.16,0:02:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And as to the matter{\i0}\N{\i1}of the Hastings ball on Friday…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.83,0:02:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}might I count on your attendance?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.41,0:02:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have little choice in the matter,{\i0}\N{\i1}seeing as I am one of the hosts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.29,0:02:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It shall be your last such commitment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.17,0:02:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This time next week,{\i0}\N{\i1}our ruse will be well and truly over.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.30,0:02:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah… Um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.63,0:02:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Apologies, but this is not working.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.34,0:02:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps His Grace might place his hand{\i0}\N{\i1}on the duchess's shoulder,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.76,0:02:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so that you both can look{\i0}\N{\i1}as happy as you surely must be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.81,0:03:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.66,0:03:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.71,0:03:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The very picture of devotion.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.30,0:03:36.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne breathes deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.78,0:03:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}-Then where did you meet her?{\i0}\N{\i1}-About town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.24,0:03:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}At her shop?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.15,0:03:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should you not be off somewhere,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.70,0:03:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}getting ready to attend{\i0}\N{\i1}your very first ball?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.53,0:03:56.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunts irritably]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.95,0:04:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Brother, might I be able to join in{\i0}\N{\i1}on the fun this summer at Aubrey Hall?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.87,0:04:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Brother!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.08,0:04:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Provided you stay clear{\i0}\N{\i1}of my lucky mallet,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.96,0:04:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think it a fine idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.09,0:04:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You cannot be in earnest.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I shall begin practicing straightaway!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.46,0:04:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What other places might Madame Delacroix{\i0}\N{\i1}frequent besides her shop?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.09,0:04:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Many places, Eloise,{\i0}\N{\i1}for her many interests.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.97,0:04:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You mean her many secrets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.27,0:04:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should be careful, Benedict.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.81,0:04:24.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Madame Delacroix{\i0}\N{\i1}may not be who you think she is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.56,0:04:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And consorting with her,{\i0}\N{\i1}well, there may be consequences.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.15,0:04:30.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would have expected this{\i0}\N{\i1}from anyone but you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.61,0:04:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You think just because{\i0}\N{\i1}Madame Delacroix has a paid occupation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.11,0:04:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or because she does not reside{\i0}\N{\i1}within Grosvenor Square,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.36,0:04:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she's different. Is that it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.95,0:04:39.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That she is somehow{\i0}\N{\i1}less deserving of my attention{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.24,0:04:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because she is not whom{\i0}\N{\i1}polite society deems appropriate?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.66,0:04:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-That is not what I am saying at all.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Then what are you saying?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.50,0:04:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are right.{\i0}\N{\i1}I should prepare for our sister's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.67,0:04:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you should.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.59,0:04:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Aunt Winnie has sent word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.30,0:04:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Francesca will be arriving home tomorrow.{\i0}\N{\i1}-How exciting!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.47,0:04:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps she can tell us{\i0}\N{\i1}of time spent far from London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.60,0:05:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Fran has missed so much.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet] Mm. Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.10,0:05:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It certainly has been an eventful season,{\i0}\N{\i1}what with Daphne and the duke,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.98,0:05:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then Anthony and…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.69,0:05:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, well, never mind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.40,0:05:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.40,0:05:15.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Marina] Pen, come in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.57,0:05:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wh-- What are you doing?{\i0}\N{\i1}Mama said you must rest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.12,0:05:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am already feeling much improved.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.66,0:05:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Marina…{\i0}\N{\i1}-What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.04,0:05:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Penelope, I assure you I am well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.79,0:05:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That tea has accomplished{\i0}\N{\i1}what I needed it to.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.67,0:05:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And now, with the season over…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.29,0:05:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tremulously] …I can finally go home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.50,0:05:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-So that means you are no longer--{\i0}\N{\i1}-With child?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.13,0:05:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would have felt something{\i0}\N{\i1}by now, I am certain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.51,0:05:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Marina sniffles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.64,0:05:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You caused quite a flutter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.81,0:05:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[quivering inhale]{\i0}\N{\i1}That was not my intention.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.31,0:05:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I am sorry{\i0}\N{\i1}for everything I have done and said.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.57,0:05:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were right about Colin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.40,0:05:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is a good man with a good heart.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.07,0:06:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were very good to him.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am certain one day he will see it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.41,0:06:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[horse driver hails]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[horse neighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.04,0:06:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is odd.{\i0}\N{\i1}We weren't expecting any callers today.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.55,0:06:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[ominous music plays]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Marina groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.84,0:06:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina? Are you quite well?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.02,0:06:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[patrons chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.48,0:06:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have made my decision.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.40,0:06:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke and I{\i0}\N{\i1}are going our separate ways.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.15,0:06:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is for the best, truly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.99,0:06:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know{\i0}\N{\i1}I do not always say the right things.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.53,0:06:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And then the things I do say, well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.53,0:06:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are not always what you wish to hear.{\i0}\N{\i1}I am only able to offer you what I know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.71,0:06:53.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}However difficult{\i0}\N{\i1}forgiving someone may be,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.46,0:06:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it is necessary to move forward.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.75,0:06:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is not up to me, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.26,0:07:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke is choosing{\i0}\N{\i1}to nurture some grudge against his father{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.64,0:07:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}instead of allowing himself any…{\i0}\N{\i1}any kind of happiness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.47,0:07:09.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}However am I supposed to forgive that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.93,0:07:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}However are we supposed to move forward{\i0}\N{\i1}from there?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.40,0:07:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington] Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.03,0:07:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do hope you are finding{\i0}\N{\i1}everything you need for Friday's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.32,0:07:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It will certainly be{\i0}\N{\i1}the event of the season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.53,0:07:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, my young ladies{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.24,0:07:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}will have to hear about{\i0}\N{\i1}the wondrous festivities the next day,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.71,0:07:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}seeing how{\i0}\N{\i1}they did not receive an invitation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.00,0:07:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prudence, in particular,{\i0}\N{\i1}is in tears about it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.25,0:07:39.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is she not, Mrs. Varley?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.67,0:07:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh! Uh…{\i0}\N{\i1}A-- Absolute watering pot, that one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.80,0:07:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you might explain{\i0}\N{\i1}to your young ladies, Lady Featherington,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.85,0:07:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}how they ended up{\i0}\N{\i1}in such an unfortunate situation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.64,0:07:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and who exactly put them there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.98,0:07:53.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or perhaps we can make room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.44,0:07:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I certainly would have no problem{\i0}\N{\i1}extending my invitation,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.19,0:08:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as I am sure all of us would like{\i0}\N{\i1}to forgive the errors of the past{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.44,0:08:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and move forward.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.78,0:08:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, Mama?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.74,0:08:07.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If that is what you wish.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.91,0:08:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How wonderful!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.95,0:08:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.20,0:08:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Apologies, ma'am, but a carriage{\i0}\N{\i1}has arrived back at the house.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.21,0:08:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A Mr. Crane is there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.17,0:08:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon,{\i0}\N{\i1}but did you say "Crane"?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.30,0:08:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would that be a Sir George Crane?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.01,0:08:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Crane, how delightful{\i0}\N{\i1}to make your acquaintance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.10,0:08:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had no idea a soldier{\i0}\N{\i1}such as yourself was coming to town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.35,0:08:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And, well, Miss Thompson has not received{\i0}\N{\i1}any correspondence from you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.73,0:08:41.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in quite some time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.69,0:08:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nor would I have expected her to, my lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.15,0:08:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.07,0:08:47.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That man is not who you believe him{\i0}\N{\i1}to be, Lady Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.70,0:08:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not George,{\i0}\N{\i1}but his brother, Sir Phillip.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.04,0:08:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sucks teeth]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.54,0:08:56.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have come bearing grim news today.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.75,0:09:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My brother George died on the battlefield…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.92,0:09:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}several weeks ago, and, uh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.84,0:09:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.64,0:09:12.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina, please, wait.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.43,0:09:16.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was writing to me…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.23,0:09:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.90,0:09:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to tell me he loved me…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.57,0:09:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to tell me we could run away together{\i0}\N{\i1}and marry and have our child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.70,0:09:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sir Phillip found this half-written letter{\i0}\N{\i1}amongst George's belongings after he, um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.34,0:09:44.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If it were not for your recent inquiries,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.09,0:09:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sir Phillip never would have known{\i0}\N{\i1}I was here,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.63,0:09:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I never would have known George…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.64,0:09:53.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He loved me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.35,0:09:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crying] All this time, he loved me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.32,0:10:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing] I thought him a villain,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.86,0:10:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he was not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.40,0:10:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.66,0:10:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He had a perfectly reasonable explanation{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.33,0:10:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for not writing back to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.04,0:10:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I was wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.06,0:10:38.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise chuckling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.52,0:10:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Genevieve sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.60,0:10:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Eloise, you should come back{\i0}\N{\i1}another day when the shop is open.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.11,0:10:47.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had hoped you would make{\i0}\N{\i1}an exception for me. [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.49,0:10:49.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need a dress for my sister's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.20,0:10:53.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You already have a dress{\i0}\N{\i1}for your sister's ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.16,0:10:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need another one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.99,0:10:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A young lady can never have{\i0}\N{\i1}too many dresses. [forced chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.83,0:11:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.38,0:11:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ooh! Perhaps this one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.59,0:11:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It would make me look quite in fashion{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.75,0:11:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in the eyes of the Featheringtons,{\i0}\N{\i1}I rather think.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.76,0:11:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Unfortunate young ladies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.59,0:11:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are still quite stung{\i0}\N{\i1}from Lady Whistledown's recent exposé.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.64,0:11:17.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish the author would write{\i0}\N{\i1}something flattering about them!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.72,0:11:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Perhaps she will.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What makes you say that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.48,0:11:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because she knows{\i0}\N{\i1}what is good for her business,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.65,0:11:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and angering loyal customers is not good.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.40,0:11:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No… No, it is not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.65,0:11:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whether those loyal customers{\i0}\N{\i1}be Featheringtons{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.53,0:11:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or Bridgertons, even…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.66,0:11:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown might wish{\i0}\N{\i1}to examine what she writes about both.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.37,0:11:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.00,0:11:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have heard people say that men,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.75,0:11:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}such as my brother, if you will,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.75,0:11:51.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}can withstand rumor and gossip,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.42,0:11:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.18,0:11:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not always so sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.10,0:11:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know why you are here, Miss Eloise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.52,0:12:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are very smart,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.31,0:12:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you care very much{\i0}\N{\i1}about the people in your life,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.85,0:12:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as you should.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.65,0:12:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But you must know I have no intention{\i0}\N{\i1}of compromising anyone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.57,0:12:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise] That is good.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.49,0:12:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because the queen is enraged.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.24,0:12:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So whoever Whistledown is{\i0}\N{\i1}should be careful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.29,0:12:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would hate her to be silenced{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.25,0:12:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}before she has a chance to change her ways{\i0}\N{\i1}and make things right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.84,0:12:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe Whistledown is smart enough{\i0}\N{\i1}to take care of herself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.51,0:12:33.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.18,0:12:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She certainly is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.30,0:12:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.22,0:12:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Charming chatting with you,{\i0}\N{\i1}Madame Delacroix.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.60,0:12:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.56,0:12:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lock the door.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.52,0:12:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[staff chattering busily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.94,0:13:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.44,0:13:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Heading to Will's boxing match?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm-hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.98,0:13:36.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Will you be accompanying me?{\i0}\N{\i1}-No. I have much to do for the ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.74,0:13:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.78,0:13:40.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But, of course, you should go{\i0}\N{\i1}and express your support.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.87,0:13:44.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.58,0:13:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What did your father do…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.79,0:13:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to make you take that vow{\i0}\N{\i1}in the first place?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.46,0:13:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We do not need to have this conversation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.17,0:13:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do I not deserve an explanation,{\i0}\N{\i1}as your wife?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.88,0:13:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You deserve more than that indeed. I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.35,0:14:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may not understand this now,{\i0}\N{\i1}but Daphne, you must know{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.73,0:14:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am doing this for your own good.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.69,0:14:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I can decide for myself what is--{\i0}\N{\i1}-You will be better off without me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.50,0:14:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.38,0:14:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[attendees clamoring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.39,0:14:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[bookmaker]{\i0}\N{\i1}Three-to-one on Iron Fist to win!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.85,0:14:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Five-to-two in favor of Iron Fist!{\i0}\N{\i1}You, sir?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.32,0:14:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Win this fight,{\i0}\N{\i1}and perhaps we leave this city.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.82,0:15:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We can take our exhibitions{\i0}\N{\i1}all over England if we wish.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.12,0:15:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To continue living fight-to-fight?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.91,0:15:08.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We should be planning{\i0}\N{\i1}for our future, Alice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.20,0:15:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot fight forever.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.33,0:15:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our circumstance is solely dependent{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.25,0:15:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on how well I can pander and grovel{\i0}\N{\i1}to the likes of…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.92,0:15:16.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.21,0:15:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Will, what are you saying?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.84,0:15:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I lose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.18,0:15:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps that purse{\i0}\N{\i1}will be enough to keep us happy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.70,0:15:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Thank you for meeting me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Always interested in a good fight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.74,0:15:49.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But why did you want us here?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.58,0:15:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want to place a sizable wager{\i0}\N{\i1}on this match,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.33,0:15:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I am told you two{\i0}\N{\i1}can manage serious transactions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.13,0:15:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My money is on The Beast.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.88,0:16:01.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] With Mondrich heavily favored?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.80,0:16:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's only one reason a flash cull lord{\i0}\N{\i1}would come to us with such a bet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.80,0:16:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anyone who knows you{\i0}\N{\i1}must know your word is worthless.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.89,0:16:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You don't need to take my word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.14,0:16:15.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Instead…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.06,0:16:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you can take the deed to my house.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.98,0:16:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I lose, it's yours.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.70,0:16:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[suspenseful music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.47,0:16:53.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I figured{\i0}\N{\i1}you'd have been here an hour ago.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.93,0:16:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I would've been,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.10,0:16:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but it's not as if you needed me here{\i0}\N{\i1}to wish you luck.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.56,0:16:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You ready?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.69,0:17:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I shall ever be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.53,0:17:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[boxing bell rings]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.57,0:17:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,{\i0}\N{\i1}take your seats!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.95,0:17:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The match is about to begin!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.62,0:17:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheers]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.96,0:17:19.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our credit at the modiste,{\i0}\N{\i1}it is still rather precarious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.96,0:17:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As in, it is nonexistent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.88,0:17:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Featherington sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.92,0:17:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The young ladies will just have{\i0}\N{\i1}to wear something they've worn before.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.09,0:17:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Before? [incredulously]{\i0}\N{\i1}Mama, I would rather not attend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.59,0:17:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can one even wear a dress worn before?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.02,0:17:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon, my lady,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.94,0:17:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but it seems{\i0}\N{\i1}my business here is not quite finished.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.35,0:17:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would very much like{\i0}\N{\i1}to speak to Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.19,0:17:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a question for her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.65,0:17:46.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marry {\i0}<span style="style2">you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.57,0:17:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.32,0:17:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After my brother{\i0}\N{\i1}clearly took liberties with your…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.83,0:17:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}virtue…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.00,0:17:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would merely be doing my duty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.04,0:18:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps] A respectable marriage!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.80,0:18:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.30,0:18:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a fine thing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.17,0:18:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sir Phillip inherited the Crane title.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.34,0:18:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He has a perfectly adequate estate{\i0}\N{\i1}to support you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.35,0:18:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and perhaps your distant cousins too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.35,0:18:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.56,0:18:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know this man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.60,0:18:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not love this man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.48,0:18:24.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot marry this man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.16,0:18:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George cared for you very much,{\i0}\N{\i1}Miss Thompson, and that will never change,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.16,0:18:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he would have wanted you{\i0}\N{\i1}to be looked after.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.41,0:18:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He would have wanted you to be supported.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.29,0:18:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Allow me{\i0}\N{\i1}to realize my late brother's wishes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.55,0:18:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thank you for your offer, Sir Phillip,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.01,0:18:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I believe{\i0}\N{\i1}you should now take your leave.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.69,0:19:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Very well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.31,0:19:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish you all the best, Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.58,0:19:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What have you done?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.37,0:19:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That was a perfectly acceptable proposal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.21,0:19:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am no longer with child,{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Featherington,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.84,0:19:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so it is neither necessary,{\i0}\N{\i1}nor acceptable, for me to participate{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.89,0:19:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in any more unwanted arrangements{\i0}\N{\i1}or disingenuous schemes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.10,0:19:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington sighs sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.80,0:20:18.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[mouthing silently]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.86,0:20:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheering raucously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.87,0:20:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come on, Will!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.33,0:20:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.00,0:20:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hit him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.88,0:20:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Knock him out!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.42,0:20:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oh, my word!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[indistinct clamoring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.09,0:20:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[blows landing] {\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.14,0:20:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Make me some money!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.65,0:21:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.48,0:21:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[no audible dialogue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.75,0:21:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dramatic music intensifies]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.25,0:21:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.10,0:21:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.52,0:21:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Siena gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.40,0:21:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.28,0:21:59.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd cheering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.28,0:22:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can do this!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.54,0:22:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come on! Come on, The Beast!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.38,0:22:12.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd] Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.80,0:22:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crowd] Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.43,0:22:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.43,0:22:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[quietly] Yeah. Yeah.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.14,0:22:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shocked exclamations]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.77,0:22:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[The Beast yells]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.10,0:22:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.90,0:22:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.82,0:22:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Get up, Mondrich!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.94,0:22:38.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I won!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.49,0:22:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shouts] I won!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.26,0:23:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[woman] Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.55,0:23:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.81,0:23:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you forget we were to come{\i0}\N{\i1}and help with preparations for your ball?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.31,0:23:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your mama is waiting in the parlor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.27,0:23:11.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall be there momentarily.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.52,0:23:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Danbury?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.28,0:23:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you know about these letters…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.95,0:23:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the ones the duke seems to have written{\i0}\N{\i1}to his father as a boy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.08,0:23:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.79,0:23:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And now, apparently, so do you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.62,0:23:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had no idea…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.83,0:23:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that Simon had trouble speaking{\i0}\N{\i1}as a child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.42,0:23:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could you have done?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.67,0:23:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He worked so very hard{\i0}\N{\i1}to eliminate the difficulty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.67,0:23:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.43,0:23:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, he was so very proud.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.93,0:23:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is why he wrote those letters{\i0}\N{\i1}in the first place.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.64,0:23:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To keep his father informed{\i0}\N{\i1}of his progress.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.81,0:23:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.35,0:23:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The late duke{\i0}\N{\i1}never even deigned to read them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.06,0:23:55.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.98,0:23:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What kind of father--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.23,0:24:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One that not only expected{\i0}\N{\i1}but demanded perfection in his son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.74,0:24:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And when that was not achieved…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.54,0:24:09.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.33,0:24:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall leave it to you to imagine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.37,0:24:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon could not be any more different{\i0}\N{\i1}from a man such as that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.59,0:24:18.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.88,0:24:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We know that to be true, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.38,0:24:23.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You helped him…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.22,0:24:26.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}overcome his…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.35,0:24:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}impediment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.35,0:24:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I merely showed him{\i0}\N{\i1}what he was capable of all along.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.39,0:24:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And if he needed some encouragement,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.10,0:24:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a push from time to time,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.44,0:24:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that was something I was happy to provide.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.98,0:24:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But at the end of the day,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.57,0:24:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the duke's triumph was his and his alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.32,0:24:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It had to be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.16,0:24:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[excited chatter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.67,0:25:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.01,0:25:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It appears I could have used{\i0}\N{\i1}that luck of yours today, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.76,0:25:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.39,0:25:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though you still managed{\i0}\N{\i1}to put on quite a performance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.27,0:25:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you needed another investor{\i0}\N{\i1}or more money, Will,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.90,0:25:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you could have come to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.28,0:25:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I appreciate the offer, friend,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I do not need your charity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.41,0:25:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What happened to your honor?{\i0}\N{\i1}-My honor?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.37,0:25:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell me, Your Grace,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.29,0:25:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}what ever could be more honorable{\i0}\N{\i1}besides taking care of one's family?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.13,0:25:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Besides doing what needs to be done?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Is that what you hope to tell Alice?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.42,0:25:45.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You truly believe{\i0}\N{\i1}she will come to understand your deceit?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.47,0:25:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you should stop worrying{\i0}\N{\i1}about my marriage,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.68,0:25:49.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and instead put your mind to your own.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.93,0:25:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-That is not what this is about.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Is it not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.89,0:25:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd be willing to wager{\i0}\N{\i1}your wife says differently.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.02,0:25:55.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Watch yourself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.35,0:26:00.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're angry,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.90,0:26:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but not with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.19,0:26:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So take it somewhere else{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.07,0:26:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and finally do something about it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.42,0:26:23.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is this?{\i0}\N{\i1}And more importantly, how did you get it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.92,0:26:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had an inside tip.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.38,0:26:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What kind of tip?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.67,0:26:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-The good kind.{\i0}\N{\i1}-But where did you--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.22,0:26:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does it matter?{\i0}\N{\i1}Portia, our problems are solved.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.64,0:26:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And this is only half the winnings.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.35,0:26:36.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Where is the other half?{\i0}\N{\i1}-I used it to pay off my man.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.31,0:26:39.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No matter,{\i0}\N{\i1}because this is more than enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.23,0:26:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Varley?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.78,0:26:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're off to the modiste{\i0}\N{\i1}straight away in the morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.11,0:26:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The young ladies{\i0}\N{\i1}shall have new dresses after all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.70,0:26:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.76,0:27:09.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought you enjoyed breakfast{\i0}\N{\i1}in the morning room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.17,0:27:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wished for different scenery today.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.84,0:27:14.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I can go if you would like.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.43,0:27:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have already begun.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.04,0:27:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is something--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.96,0:27:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm going to Bridgerton House{\i0}\N{\i1}this morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.71,0:27:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dear Francesca has returned from Bath.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.38,0:27:53.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It seems my entire family is gathering.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.55,0:27:56.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you care to join me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.93,0:28:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must admit, my brothers{\i0}\N{\i1}will think it odd if you do not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.60,0:28:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.15,0:28:08.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, I shall join you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.74,0:28:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] I am confident I could last{\i0}\N{\i1}a few rounds in a boxing ring.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:19.74,0:28:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, that is certainly{\i0}\N{\i1}a match I would like to see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.33,0:28:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sister! [gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.12,0:28:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Francesca! Welcome home.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is so wonderful to see you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.34,0:28:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.09,0:28:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought four brothers enough,{\i0}\N{\i1}but returning to five is quite nice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.38,0:28:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simon!{\i0}\N{\i1}When will {\i0}<span style="style2">I {\i0}{\i1}be able to visit Clyvedon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.39,0:28:38.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Allow the duke to find a seat{\i0}\N{\i1}before you trouble him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.85,0:28:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are welcome to visit at any time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.89,0:28:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.64,0:28:45.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, come. Show me{\i0}\N{\i1}what you've been learning all summer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.65,0:28:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not share my food.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.98,0:28:50.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are not to do{\i0}\N{\i1}what you did the other morning ever again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.44,0:28:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you understand, Eloise?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.28,0:28:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You mean visiting my new acquaintance?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.86,0:28:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-She is not your acquaintance.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I was wrong about her. She is wonderful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.70,0:28:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You have nothing to worry about.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I wasn't worried about anything.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.33,0:29:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not worried about what?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.37,0:29:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Uh…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.66,0:29:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.17,0:29:08.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a friendship{\i0}\N{\i1}with Genevieve Delacroix…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.54,0:29:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.80,0:29:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…the…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.46,0:29:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}modiste.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.26,0:29:23.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good for you, Brother.{\i0}\N{\i1}You deserve contentment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.14,0:29:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We all do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.18,0:29:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If the lady contributes to that,{\i0}\N{\i1}then I'm happy for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.77,0:29:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Sister,{\i0}\N{\i1}your pianoforte is quite impressive.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.44,0:29:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Join me, Brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:30.57,0:29:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Violet] Yes, Colin, why not a song?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Colin] If I must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.44,0:29:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever is in those candies?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.11,0:29:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colin]{\i0}\N{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">Now we are met, let mirth abound ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.95,0:29:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">And let the catch and toast go round ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.37,0:29:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">And then the catch, and then the catch ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.12,0:29:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Gregory] Spin!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.70,0:29:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">And let the catch and toast go round ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.37,0:29:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">Now we are met, let mirth around ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.80,0:29:53.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">And let the catch and toast go round ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.46,0:29:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth] Move!{\i0}\N{\i1}I want to dance with the duke.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.80,0:29:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And then the catch, and then the catch ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.51,0:30:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-♪ {\i0}<span style="style2">And let the catch and toast go round ♪{\i0}\N{\i1}-I have news.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.39,0:30:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I finally found her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.93,0:30:06.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Lady Whistledown.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Who is she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.85,0:30:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is Madame Delacroix.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.44,0:30:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Madame Delacroix is her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.27,0:30:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The modiste and Whistledown{\i0}\N{\i1}are one and the same.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.57,0:30:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And she is going to print something{\i0}\N{\i1}in your family's favor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.94,0:30:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She told me so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.15,0:30:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, that certainly{\i0}\N{\i1}is an impressive feat,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.82,0:30:19.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}running two businesses.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.91,0:30:23.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We should both aspire to be just like her:{\i0}\N{\i1}Unmarried, earning our own money.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:23.54,0:30:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look, I'm happy you found her, El,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.66,0:30:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I do not think{\i0}\N{\i1}I can ever be like that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.71,0:30:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You now have a duchess for a sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.75,0:30:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That makes achieving{\i0}\N{\i1}the life you wish for all the more easier.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.96,0:30:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The status of my family, however,{\i0}\N{\i1}is an entirely different story,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.17,0:30:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which will not be changing{\i0}\N{\i1}in the foreseeable future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.89,0:30:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth] Yes, Colin!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.14,0:30:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colin]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">♪ And let the catch and toast go round ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.81,0:30:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And let the catch, and let the catch ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.98,0:30:51.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}♪ And let the catch and toast go round{\i0}<span style="style1"> ♪{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.90,0:30:53.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests clapping, cheering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.90,0:30:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And exactly how many horses do you have?{\i0}\N{\i1}Might I have an extra one?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.65,0:30:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your horses are the prettiest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.90,0:31:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe the duke has heard enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:00.70,0:31:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would a pony do?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.12,0:31:04.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[laughs] I could not fathom…{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet] Your Grace!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.96,0:31:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, here's the tricky one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.79,0:31:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.75,0:31:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth, Gregory laugh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.42,0:31:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do realize it is only made of paper?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.72,0:31:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.05,0:31:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[imitates horse nickering]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Gregory laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.01,0:31:24.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon imitates horse trotting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.89,0:31:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Hyacinth laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.27,0:31:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington gasps]{\i0}\N{\i1}Oh! Astonishing, Madame Delacroix!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.10,0:31:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because you were able{\i0}\N{\i1}to pay in advance this time,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.15,0:31:38.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and since I happened to have{\i0}\N{\i1}some fabrics no one else seemed to want…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:38.86,0:31:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There are two others just like it,{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.32,0:31:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mine will have to be taken in, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.70,0:31:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mine's perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.16,0:31:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And mine is yellow.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.37,0:31:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You see, young ladies,{\i0}\N{\i1}everything works out in the end.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.12,0:31:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And Philipa, perhaps Mr. Finch{\i0}\N{\i1}might even reconsider his proposal,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.92,0:31:58.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}now that, um, you have your dowry again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.92,0:32:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Again?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.72,0:32:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, did I lose it somewhere{\i0}\N{\i1}the first time?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.59,0:32:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chattering, laughter continue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.48,0:32:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps approach]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.86,0:32:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.15,0:32:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.24,0:32:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.78,0:32:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe I need a doctor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.41,0:32:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">The final ball of any season{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.08,0:32:31.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is distinguished by one of two things,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.62,0:32:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}anticipation…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.37,0:32:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or dread.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.19,0:33:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For, while those who have been successful{\i0}\N{\i1}in the year's marriage market{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.12,0:33:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}look forward to flaunting{\i0}\N{\i1}their perfect, joyous unions…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.29,0:33:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}others shudder at the thought{\i0}\N{\i1}of spending one last night{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.17,0:33:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}before the discerning eyes of the ton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.55,0:33:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As they know, indeed,{\i0}\N{\i1}just what the evening signifies,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.89,0:33:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that their time is officially up.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.31,0:33:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Featherington]{\i0}\N{\i1}So, does that mean--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.94,0:33:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You truly believed{\i0}\N{\i1}a tea would rectify the situation, madam?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.44,0:33:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs] As if that ever works.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.44,0:33:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown] {\i0}<span style="style2">And yet, to those{\i0}\N<span style="style2">who may still find themselves{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.82,0:33:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}out of both choices and hope, fear not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.04,0:33:56.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For who knows when{\i0}\N{\i1}and where one's fortunes may change?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.16,0:33:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-He was… He was completely in his cups!{\i0}\N{\i1}-[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.50,0:34:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd wager the both of you were.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:03.38,0:34:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And I would take your bet.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Siena giggles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:06.17,0:34:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oh…{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Anthony kissing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.93,0:34:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Siena moans lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:14.18,0:34:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We must part.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.77,0:34:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should prepare for my show.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.98,0:34:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.27,0:34:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I believe there is{\i0}\N{\i1}a ball somewhere requiring your presence.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.57,0:34:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The last one, yes?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.78,0:34:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of the season.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.28,0:34:28.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though… [clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.70,0:34:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…unfortunately, not the last of mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.24,0:34:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does that mean{\i0}\N{\i1}you'll dance tonight, my lord?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.54,0:34:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Anthony chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Perhaps a quadrille?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.16,0:34:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, do not tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}you shall find some young lady{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.46,0:34:42.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to lead in a waltz all evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:42.88,0:34:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall not be{\i0}\N{\i1}anywhere near that dance floor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.76,0:34:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.13,0:34:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At least, not if I have a say in it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.09,0:34:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, wherever is the fun in that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.90,0:35:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I shall--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Come with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.94,0:35:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.15,0:35:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Siena, I am a viscount.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.90,0:35:11.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My sister is now a duchess,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.70,0:35:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and the duke my brother-in-law.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.12,0:35:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is no one{\i0}\N{\i1}that would dare say a thing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.74,0:35:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[scoffs] No, not to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.33,0:35:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is preposterous and fantastical.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.09,0:35:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And you know it.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I want you there by my side.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.51,0:35:34.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[softly] Come with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.06,0:35:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.86,0:35:46.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both gasping, laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.13,0:36:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-A good likeness.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon] Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.05,0:36:18.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though Mr. Granville did seem to omit{\i0}\N{\i1}the gray hair or two I've surely gained{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.39,0:36:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from the emotions of the past few weeks.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.31,0:36:21.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.31,0:36:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Perhaps a few wrinkles too.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh! You wound me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.44,0:36:32.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We should discuss{\i0}\N{\i1}the order of events this evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.28,0:36:33.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Naturally.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.65,0:36:38.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think it wise for us to engage{\i0}\N{\i1}in three dances, would you say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.28,0:36:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Two.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is our ball, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.08,0:36:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do fear two dances{\i0}\N{\i1}may leave our guests terribly unexcited.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.92,0:36:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is better than the opposite,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.59,0:36:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}leaving them overly excited{\i0}\N{\i1}and terribly unruly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.75,0:36:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Two dances at most.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.67,0:36:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.02,0:37:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were wonderful today{\i0}\N{\i1}with Gregory and Hyacinth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.31,0:37:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They adore you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.48,0:37:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Children always have done.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:12.78,0:37:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It still does not mean{\i0}\N{\i1}I want any of my own.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.32,0:37:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.04,0:37:23.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Graces, your guests are arriving.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.21,0:37:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One last dance, it is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.22,0:37:39.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering excitedly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:42.64,0:37:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[light waltz music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.99,0:37:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[indistinct chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.90,0:38:33.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you should like{\i0}\N{\i1}to paint a picture?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.78,0:38:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.24,0:38:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dearest, you must see this as a rehearsal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.62,0:38:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Until you are officially out,{\i0}\N{\i1}you need not feel so strained tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.58,0:38:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As if I shall feel anything{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.70,0:38:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but the inability to breathe{\i0}\N{\i1}in this corset.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.62,0:38:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My dear… [chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.38,0:38:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For someone who hates ballgowns…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.63,0:38:58.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you look exquisite in one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.26,0:39:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yeah.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.10,0:39:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you wish to go up to the library{\i0}\N{\i1}for the rest of the evening,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.72,0:39:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall not say a word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.60,0:39:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nor shall I blame you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.52,0:39:11.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am merely glad you came.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.23,0:39:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sister…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.49,0:39:18.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I should thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.03,0:39:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[scoffs] Whatever for?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.16,0:39:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For being so perfect…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:24.28,0:39:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so I do not have to be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.13,0:39:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh! Look who's here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.68,0:39:43.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Philipa gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.97,0:39:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Featherington,{\i0}\N{\i1}what a pleasant surprise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.73,0:39:53.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We did not expect to see you here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.27,0:39:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What can I say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.98,0:39:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duchess extended{\i0}\N{\i1}an invitation personally.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.78,0:40:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Circumstances change, ladies.{\i0}\N{\i1}Sometimes overnight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.20,0:40:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We hear your husband{\i0}\N{\i1}secured himself a win the other day.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.03,0:40:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where is he? Still out celebrating?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.62,0:40:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One circumstance{\i0}\N{\i1}that has most likely not changed,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.20,0:40:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I imagine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.17,0:40:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[raucous laughter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.13,0:40:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone special in here for me, I presume?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.71,0:40:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only the best for you, my lord.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.22,0:40:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[ominous music plays]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[man] Featherington.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.14,0:40:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Join us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.07,0:40:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[music and chattering continue]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.88,0:41:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Enjoying your evening?{\i0}\N{\i1}-What?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.59,0:41:07.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you enjoying your evening?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.18,0:41:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah… Y-- Yes.{\i0}\N{\i1}I just came from the dance floor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.97,0:41:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not see you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.52,0:41:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was in the back of the dance floor.{\i0}\N{\i1}It was quite crowded,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.52,0:41:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}so… [chuckles nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.56,0:41:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Colin--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Pen--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.77,0:41:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope chuckles nervously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:22.36,0:41:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I owe you an apology.{\i0}\N{\i1}I did not see it at first,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.53,0:41:27.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I know you were only trying{\i0}\N{\i1}to prevent me from heartache{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.91,0:41:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with Miss Thompson, and…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.20,0:41:31.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:31.33,0:41:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-And I was a fool.{\i0}\N{\i1}-You were not a fool.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.54,0:41:36.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You merely believed yourself in love.{\i0}\N{\i1}One should never apologize for that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.21,0:41:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}One finds oneself{\i0}\N{\i1}in such an incredible position,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.21,0:41:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and, well, one should declare it…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:43.63,0:41:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}assuredly, fervently…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:47.59,0:41:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}loudly.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.39,0:41:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colin, I wish to tell you something.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.14,0:41:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have something{\i0}\N{\i1}I wish to tell you as well, Pen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.02,0:41:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am leaving.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.86,0:42:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}First thing tomorrow morning,{\i0}\N{\i1}I begin my tour.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.07,0:42:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am to start in the Mediterranean.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.03,0:42:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was actually you who inspired me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:08.53,0:42:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You kept reminding me{\i0}\N{\i1}how much I longed for travel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.66,0:42:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, um… What was it you wished to say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.33,0:42:16.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't remember. [clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.25,0:42:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Shall we dance, Pen?{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.62,0:42:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Um… I am all danced out{\i0}\N{\i1}for the night, Colin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:23.21,0:42:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Good luck on your tour.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.97,0:42:35.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise] Pen!{\i0}\N{\i1}Look, the queen. She is here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.68,0:42:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now is my chance{\i0}\N{\i1}to find out her plans for Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.81,0:42:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, is everything all right?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.19,0:42:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Entirely all right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.23,0:42:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The queen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.74,0:42:48.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go before you miss your chance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.82,0:42:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.83,0:42:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:55.41,0:42:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[chuckles lightly]{\i0}\N{\i1}-One does not approach Her Majesty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.16,0:43:00.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I require an audience.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:00.33,0:43:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oh, well, in that case…{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Eloise chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.04,0:43:02.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:05.63,0:43:06.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I only wish to thank her{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.88,0:43:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for the opportunity{\i0}\N{\i1}to investigate Whistledown on her behalf.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:10.26,0:43:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I imagine she must be coming close{\i0}\N{\i1}to unmasking the author's identity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.55,0:43:16.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Especially now she has engaged{\i0}\N{\i1}such esteemed counsel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.89,0:43:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have no idea.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.27,0:43:21.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We shall unmask her this very night.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.98,0:43:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.48,0:43:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course you shall.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.44,0:43:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That team of Bow Street Runners{\i0}\N{\i1}was all your brilliance, was it not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:28.61,0:43:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.53,0:43:34.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her Majesty is lucky to have you,{\i0}\N{\i1}a man of such talent, such genius.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:35.91,0:43:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We worked out{\i0}\N{\i1}that Whistledown delivers her missives{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.04,0:43:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to a printers press on Lombard Street,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.33,0:43:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}all when the rest of society is distracted{\i0}\N{\i1}by big events, like this one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:44.50,0:43:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is how she operates.{\i0}\N{\i1}She will be seized there tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.34,0:43:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Queen Charlotte] Brimsley! I need you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.43,0:43:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh my…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.35,0:43:56.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Brother, you must see to Genevieve.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.26,0:43:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Ensure she stays home tonight.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Eloise, not now!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.86,0:44:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:07.90,0:44:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:12.36,0:44:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I need you to take me somewhere.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Miss Eloise--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:15.12,0:44:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have pin money…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.99,0:44:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a great deal of it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.23,0:44:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Oh.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Apologies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.32,0:44:49.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Siena] My lord…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:50.53,0:44:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps approaching]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.49,0:44:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give me a moment, my love,{\i0}\N{\i1}and I shall return upstairs.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.12,0:45:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales tremulously]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.13,0:45:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought about coming with you tonight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:15.26,0:45:17.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I envisioned myself on your arm…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:19.26,0:45:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}dancing the entire night away.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.64,0:45:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But my imagination was{\i0}\N{\i1}the furthest I could allow myself to go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.10,0:45:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Siena, what are you doing?{\i0}\N{\i1}-What am I doing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.61,0:45:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What am I--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.49,0:45:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am doing the very thing{\i0}\N{\i1}I have always done.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.28,0:45:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am looking out for myself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.58,0:45:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am ensuring my own future.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:43.08,0:45:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I know…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.62,0:45:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in my heart…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.54,0:45:52.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know{\i0}\N{\i1}that there is no one else who ever will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:54.51,0:45:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I tried.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.84,0:45:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must know, I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.01,0:46:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I tried.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.93,0:46:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I know is that you are lost.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.56,0:46:09.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I cannot allow you{\i0}\N{\i1}to set me adrift as well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.52,0:46:11.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.65,0:46:17.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need to let me go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.20,0:46:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I know I have been unfair--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Let me go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:30.13,0:46:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am comfortable.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.59,0:46:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am content.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.80,0:46:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That gentleman upstairs…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.76,0:46:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}he sees me for who I am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.76,0:46:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Unlike you, he does not wish{\i0}\N{\i1}for me to don some ridiculous gown{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.23,0:46:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and go with him to some absurd ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.23,0:46:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He does not wish for me to change.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:56.99,0:46:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And neither do I.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.24,0:47:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You need to let me go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.63,0:47:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're right. [sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.47,0:47:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sorry, Siena.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.22,0:47:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm so sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.22,0:48:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-We must get back to the party.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Another moment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:16.19,0:48:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horse neighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:26.41,0:48:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.37,0:48:28.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.88,0:48:43.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go! It is a trap!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.88,0:48:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[driver exclaims]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[horses neigh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.93,0:48:48.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What do you think you're doing?{\i0}\N{\i1}-I apologize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:48.10,0:48:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… I thought you were someone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.43,0:48:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps you might catch up with her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.39,0:48:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.72,0:49:31.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I presume your plans to separate{\i0}\N{\i1}from Her Grace have not yet changed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.35,0:49:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They have not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:34.23,0:49:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Neither, it appears, has your ability{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.77,0:49:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to somehow hear of every piece of gossip{\i0}\N{\i1}that transpires in this town.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.19,0:49:40.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When will you accept it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.82,0:49:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.86,0:49:46.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pride, Your Grace…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.74,0:49:50.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it will cost you everything{\i0}\N{\i1}and leave you with nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.12,0:49:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must not allow it{\i0}\N{\i1}to happen to you too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:03.92,0:50:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Is it different for them, men…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.72,0:50:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to know whether they are in love?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.85,0:50:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Everything else seems different to them.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Violet chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.10,0:50:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We agreed to one dance tonight, a waltz.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.11,0:50:27.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I miss dancing with your father.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.03,0:50:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The very last time I danced was with him,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:31.78,0:50:32.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at a ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.95,0:50:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There were peacocks present, I believe.{\i0}\N{\i1}Real ones.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:36.16,0:50:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.25,0:50:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose{\i0}\N{\i1}I miss everything about him, really.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.63,0:50:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The two of you{\i0}\N{\i1}loved each other so very much.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.22,0:50:50.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a rarity, I have come to realize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.68,0:50:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is not to say{\i0}\N{\i1}it was without its trials.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.68,0:50:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your-- Your father and I faced{\i0}\N{\i1}many difficulties, indeed,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.35,0:50:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but we overcame them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.90,0:51:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We made a decision early on to do so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.31,0:51:04.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama, I do not think--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.15,0:51:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We chose{\i0}\N{\i1}to love each other every single day.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.45,0:51:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a choice, dearest,{\i0}\N{\i1}one that is never too late to make.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:16.95,0:51:21.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I may never be able{\i0}\N{\i1}to see your father again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:21.50,0:51:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I-- I may wake every morning{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.09,0:51:28.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and… and touch the pillow{\i0}\N{\i1}where he used to lay his head.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.05,0:51:33.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But knowing{\i0}\N{\i1}that the two of us made the choice to love{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.22,0:51:35.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and to do all that we could…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:37.39,0:51:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.02,0:51:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot tell you how much peace{\i0}\N{\i1}and comfort that brings to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.69,0:51:48.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales tremulously]{\i0}\N{\i1}I wish there was something, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.69,0:51:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps] I wish I could do this--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.74,0:51:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are a Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.99,0:51:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is nothing you cannot do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.49,0:51:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:13.34,0:52:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[waltz music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.57,0:53:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[thunder clapping loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.65,0:53:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:14.28,0:53:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests exclaiming]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.16,0:53:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.83,0:53:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:59.12,0:54:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everyone…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:01.24,0:54:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe this evening is complete.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:03.91,0:54:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We shall thank our gracious hosts{\i0}\N{\i1}for such a splendid soiree in the morning.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.79,0:54:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.17,0:54:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Out.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:14.67,0:54:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At once.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.39,0:54:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Daphne…{\i0}\N{\i1}-[laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.81,0:54:26.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am so sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:26.27,0:54:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For what?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:28.48,0:54:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even a duke cannot control the weather.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:30.81,0:54:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know that this is not{\i0}\N{\i1}what you had envisioned for the evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.65,0:54:35.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Certainly not.{\i0}\N{\i1}-And for that, I--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:35.90,0:54:36.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is better.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.78,0:54:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know{\i0}\N{\i1}why you made that vow to your father.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.91,0:54:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I found the letters you wrote to him{\i0}\N{\i1}as a child, and I read them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.37,0:54:50.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:50.29,0:54:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just because something is not perfect…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.05,0:54:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}does not make it any less worthy of love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:58.76,0:55:00.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your father made you believe otherwise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:02.43,0:55:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He made you believe{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.10,0:55:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that you needed to be without fault{\i0}\N{\i1}in order to be loved, but he was wrong.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:09.52,0:55:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should you need any proof{\i0}\N{\i1}of the matter, then…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:12.11,0:55:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then look just here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:15.07,0:55:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am tired of pretending.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:20.28,0:55:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I cannot continue acting as if I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:23.74,0:55:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As if I do not love you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:26.70,0:55:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.29,0:55:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I love all of you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.25,0:55:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even the parts that you believe{\i0}\N{\i1}are too dark and too shameful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.05,0:55:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every scar.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:38.67,0:55:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every flaw.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.30,0:55:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every imperfection.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.47,0:55:43.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I love you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:45.68,0:55:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may think{\i0}\N{\i1}you are too damaged and too broken{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.43,0:55:52.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to ever allow yourself to be happy,{\i0}\N{\i1}but you can choose differently, Simon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:54.52,0:55:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can choose to love me{\i0}\N{\i1}as much as I love you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.32,0:56:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That should not be up to anyone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.82,0:56:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That cannot be up to anyone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.83,0:56:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It can only be up to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.58,0:56:12.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.17,0:56:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[thunder rolls]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:33.31,0:56:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Finch has such a warm countenance,{\i0}\N{\i1}does he not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.98,0:56:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And his gaze, it inspires me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.07,0:56:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps it might inspire you into silence.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:41.07,0:56:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prudence, be kind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:42.36,0:56:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will have plenty of opportunities{\i0}\N{\i1}to find your match this summer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.32,0:56:49.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am thinking a full renovation{\i0}\N{\i1}of our country house is in order this--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.37,0:56:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where is Miss Thompson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.59,0:57:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, my lady. There is news.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.13,0:57:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What is the matter?{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is your husband, ma'am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.22,0:57:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They are saying he is dead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.73,0:57:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Bow Street Runners have questions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:35.37,0:57:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.67,0:57:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:44.84,0:57:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.18,0:57:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[wailing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.99,0:58:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[floorboard creaking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.66,0:58:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not want to be alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.33,0:58:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know that now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.25,0:58:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But what I do not know{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.88,0:58:21.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is how to be the man you need me to be…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.42,0:58:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the man you truly deserve.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.22,0:58:28.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not know how to do this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.64,0:58:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.39,0:58:31.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You do.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.80,0:58:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.68,0:58:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You stay.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.48,0:58:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You stay,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.77,0:58:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and we get through this…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:42.15,0:58:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}together.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.11,0:58:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-If you do this, if we do this, then--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Then nothing else will matter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.93,0:59:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, moaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.24,1:00:11.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both breathing heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.08,1:00:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:22.83,1:00:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:24.46,1:00:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.77,1:00:48.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:48.52,1:00:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">If there is to ever be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.07,1:00:53.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a grander finish to a season{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:53.24,1:00:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than the one provided by the Duke{\i0}\N{\i1}and Duchess of Hastings this year,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.91,1:01:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}this author will need{\i0}\N{\i1}to feast upon her own words.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:03.54,1:01:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For it was this couple's memorable affair{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:06.88,1:01:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that brought another scandalous{\i0}\N{\i1}London season to a close.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:13.22,1:01:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As many now leave the city behind{\i0}\N{\i1}for greener pastures,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:17.93,1:01:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}some endings seem{\i0}\N{\i1}more permanent than others.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:22.43,1:01:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope sobbing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:28.27,1:01:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sniffles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:34.49,1:01:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am here, Pen,{\i0}\N{\i1}to help you to find a reason, every day,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:39.53,1:01:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to endure the absence of your dear papa.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:43.66,1:01:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know… I know you will miss him.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.75,1:01:48.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Share something good.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:49.09,1:01:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What happened with Whistledown?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.96,1:01:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you save Madame Delacroix?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.01,1:01:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:57.18,1:01:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And now she will be able to put right{\i0}\N{\i1}what she botched this season,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.97,1:02:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure of it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.47,1:02:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}With Whistledown still on the loose,{\i0}\N{\i1}next season will be far more interesting.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:26.33,1:02:27.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did you do it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.46,1:02:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did you endure{\i0}\N{\i1}two and 20 years of marriage without love?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:34.96,1:02:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You find things to love, my dear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:39.47,1:02:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Small things.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.26,1:02:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Big things, too, like your babies,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.26,1:02:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and eventually they add up to be enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.60,1:02:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are strong, Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:52.02,1:02:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps even more so than me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:56.65,1:02:57.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will do well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.64,1:03:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Of course, there are other endings{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:29.98,1:03:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that will offer new beginnings…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:33.69,1:03:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horse and carriage receding]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.37,1:03:45.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell me you have a name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:45.99,1:03:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, we located him, ma'am,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:48.00,1:03:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the man who will inherit{\i0}\N{\i1}the Featherington estate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:51.29,1:03:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:53.33,1:03:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:55.29,1:03:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}look.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.51,1:04:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">…however uncertain{\i0}{\i1} {\i0}<span style="style2">those new beginnings{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.72,1:04:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}might be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:07.01,1:04:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall write to you all from Greece.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.60,1:04:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Do not forget to bring me a gift.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is not a gift if you have to ask.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.56,1:04:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I would fancy anything blue or white.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[group chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.91,1:04:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anthony, I do not recall{\i0}\N{\i1}seeing you last night.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:32.42,1:04:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes. I was feeling rather unwell.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:34.71,1:04:35.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My apologies, Sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:35.88,1:04:37.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:37.13,1:04:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The two of you are now off to Clyvedon,{\i0}\N{\i1}I presume?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:39.63,1:04:42.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have decided{\i0}\N{\i1}to stay in London a little longer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:42.97,1:04:45.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Take some time to enjoy ourselves,{\i0}\N{\i1}just the two of us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.22,1:04:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you? What are your plans, Brother?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:50.43,1:04:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nothing of note.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:51.73,1:04:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Other than finding{\i0}\N{\i1}and promptly declaring my intentions{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:54.56,1:04:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to my new viscountess, of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:57.02,1:05:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The viscount is ready to find{\i0}\N{\i1}and declare his intentions?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.61,1:05:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you hear that, Your Grace?{\i0}\N{\i1}And which young lady?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.65,1:05:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony] Does it matter?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:06.03,1:05:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have finally determined the difficulty…{\i0}\N{\i1}Love itself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:09.79,1:05:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Removing it from all romantic relations{\i0}\N{\i1}shall make me all the better for it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:13.21,1:05:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No more distractions from responsibility{\i0}\N{\i1}or being waylaid from the sensible path.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.88,1:05:20.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At any rate, enjoy your time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:23.17,1:05:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps he will learn.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.09,1:05:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps not.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.68,1:05:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Give my regards to Madame Delacroix.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your regards will have to wait, El.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.44,1:05:37.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is making a short trip back to France.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.15,1:05:38.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:38.27,1:05:40.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you not going to say goodbye to her?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:40.40,1:05:42.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did. Last night, if you must know.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.69,1:05:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We went to a party together,{\i0}\N{\i1}a very good party.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:45.70,1:05:47.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You were with Madame Delacroix last night?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:47.91,1:05:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.99,1:05:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, please do not tell our sister{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:50.87,1:05:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that I left{\i0}\N{\i1}in the middle of the ball, either.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:55.33,1:05:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.50,1:06:01.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you were with Madame Delacroix{\i0}\N{\i1}last night, then she is not-- Then…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:01.13,1:06:02.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she cannot be…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.26,1:06:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Lady Whistledown] {\i0}<span style="style2">And yet…{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh dear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:06.13,1:06:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…{\i0}<span style="style2">there is no ending in sight{\i0}\N<span style="style2">for this author,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.35,1:06:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}who recently became aware{\i0}\N{\i1}of a scheme to unmask her…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.39,1:06:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.94,1:06:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Go! It is a trap!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:21.11,1:06:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[driver exclaims]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[horses neigh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:23.65,1:06:26.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}…by one worthy opponent, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:29.74,1:06:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I will come forward one day.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:34.20,1:06:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, you must know, dear reader,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.62,1:06:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the decision shall be left{\i0}\N{\i1}entirely up to me.{\i0}
